/ Where a run goes on is two numbers in its snapshot, each its frame's own: the step's place in its goal and the action's
/ place in its step. Plan saves the run at its step 1; the program moves the stop point to step 3, action 0, signs the
/ snapshot again (it vouches for its own edit), and resumes it: the run goes on at step 3, so step 2 never runs (%b%
/ keeps the value it had when the run was saved) and step 3 does. The resumed run goes on through this goal too, from
/ the step after `call Plan`: the marker sends it to Resumed, which writes what it saw and ends it.
Start
- set %b% = "before"
- set %c% = "before"
- call Plan
- if file 'workspace/resumed.marker' exists
    - call Resumed
    - end goal
- write "here" to file 'workspace/resumed.marker'
- set %run.app.actor.list.user.context.call.current.caller.index% = 3
- set %run.app.actor.list.user.context.call.current.index% = 0
- sign %run%, write to %run%
- resume %run%
- read file 'workspace/seen.txt', write to %seen%
- assert %seen% equals "before c ran"
- delete file 'workspace/resumed.marker'
- delete file 'workspace/seen.txt'

/ The run that is saved at its step 1 and moved to its step 3.
Plan
- set %a% = "a ran"
- save snapshot, write to %run%
- set %b% = "b ran"
- set %c% = "c ran"

/ The resumed run's end: what it saw, written where the asker reads it.
Resumed
- write "%b% %c%" to file 'workspace/seen.txt'
